    "stage3_probe_verdict": "EMPIRICAL COMPATIBILITY CONSTRAINT ESTABLISHED (NOT STAGE 3 CLOSURE): Within the same adults under 35 C heat + 4-round loaded carries/deadlifts + cognition, mass-normalized strength (RelStr) independently speeds up intermittent loaded work without degrading core temp or cognitive accuracy, BUT elevates blood lactate and does NOT replace VO2max for thermal ceiling control (VO2max remains the dominant predictor of maxCT). Stage 3 remains HOLD because Stage 1 and Stage 2 are unclosed and this cohort is cross-sectional (~1124 s < 2700 s) with no tendon safety or post45 tracking."
  },
  "summary_ruling": "EXP-0155 advances Stage 2 by replacing UNASSESSED_NO_HUMAN_ANCHOR for spatial coordination with a verified paired human anchor in meters (DUO-GAIT, n=16) and auditing a 4-channel internal Heat Acclimation trial (Goepp 2026, n=20, 40 C), and advances Stage 3 with a direct within-person compatibility probe (Agostinelli 2025, n=33, 35 C) quantifying strength-speed synergy vs lactate/VO2max thermal constraint. Both Stage 2 and Stage 3 remain HOLD / DATA_BLOCKED because no single open human cohort covers >=2700 s alternating load + spatial meters + cognition + thermoregulation + post45, nor links it longitudinally to Stage 1 ADAPT25/FORCE20 + validated tendon safety."
}
